# Distributions the HDR extras are prebuilt for, one per line:
#   name                 container image               family    desktops
# The name goes into the release file names (Umbra-HDR-KDE-<name>.tar.gz). Each build takes the
# distribution's own current kwin or mutter source package and adds the patch for its version
# series (README.md lists which series exist). Not here, because no patch can cover them:
#   Debian 13, openSUSE Leap 16.0: KWin 6.3/6.4 and Mutter 48 lack the colour-managed screencast
#   the patches extend. Fedora 43: its PipeWire (1.4) has no PQ transfer function for the 10-bit
#   capture to announce (PipeWire 1.6 has it), and its Mutter 49 no HDR screen capture.
# The cachyos image needs an x86-64-v3 CPU to run; its packages are built for any x86-64 CPU.
ubuntu26.04            ubuntu:26.04                  deb       kde gnome
ubuntu26.10            ubuntu:26.10                  deb       kde gnome
fedora44               fedora:44                     fedora    kde gnome
# fedora45 gnome is left out of the 0.5.2 release build (2026-10-15): its mirrors served the Mutter 51.1 package
# but only the 51.0 source, so build.sh refused it. It is attached to the release separately once it builds.
fedora45               fedora:45                     fedora    kde
arch                   archlinux:latest              arch      kde gnome
cachyos                cachyos/cachyos-v3:latest     cachyos   kde gnome
opensuse-tumbleweed    opensuse/tumbleweed:latest    opensuse  kde gnome
